Command:
BASE=http://127.0.0.1:5000
# Set PASSWORD to the one-time test-only value; this keeps the bearer token out
# of the evidence file and mints a fresh one for the same session.
TOKEN=$(curl -sS -X POST "$BASE/login" \
  -H 'Content-Type: application/json' \
  -d "{\"username\":\"submission_evidence\",\"password\":\"$PASSWORD\"}" \
  | node -pe 'JSON.parse(require("fs").readFileSync(0,"utf8")).token')
curl -sS -X PUT "$BASE/auth/review/1" \
  -H 'Content-Type: application/json' \
  -H "Authorization: Bearer $TOKEN" \
  -d '{"review":"A thoughtful classic for the submission test."}'

The bearer token was obtained from the login response in the same local test
session and is intentionally not included in this committed evidence file.

Actual response:
{"message":"Review added successfully","review":"A thoughtful classic for the submission test."}
